# Next.js Best Practices

## App Router Architecture

- Use App Router directory structure (`app/` directory)
- Place route-specific components within route directories
- Use `loading.tsx`, `error.tsx`, and `not-found.tsx` appropriately
- Implement proper nested layouts and templates
- Use route groups for organization without affecting URLs

## Server vs Client Components

- Use Server Components by default for better performance
- Mark Client Components explicitly with 'use client'
- Minimize Client Component boundary surface area
- Pass serializable props between Server and Client Components
- Use Server Actions for form submissions and mutations

## Data Fetching Patterns

- Fetch data in Server Components when possible
- Use proper cache strategies (`force-cache`, `no-store`)
- Implement streaming with Suspense boundaries
- Use parallel data fetching patterns
- Handle loading and error states at appropriate levels

## Routing & Navigation

- Use `Link` component for client-side navigation
- Implement proper dynamic routes with `[slug]` syntax
- Use route handlers (`route.ts`) for API endpoints
- Implement proper middleware for authentication/redirects
- Handle route parameters and search params correctly

## Image & Asset Optimization

- Use `next/image` component for automatic optimization
- Implement proper `alt` attributes and sizing
- Use WebP format with fallbacks
- Configure image domains in `next.config.js`
- Implement proper lazy loading strategies

## Deployment & Configuration

- Configure `next.config.js` for production optimizations
- Use environment variables properly
- Implement proper build caching strategies
- Configure middleware for edge runtime when appropriate
- Set up proper monitoring and error tracking

- Use React Context sparingly
- Prefer server state when possible
- Implement proper loading states
